# A *path*, not an origin, and that is the whole design: `vercel.json` rewrites
# /api/* to the Render service, so the browser only ever talks to the frontend's
# own origin. The auth cookies are SameSite=Strict — under a cross-site pair
# (Vercel + *.onrender.com) login would return 200 and every request after it
# would 401. Render only sells custom domains on paid instances, so the API
# cannot join samuelsantana.dev; proxying makes the question moot instead,
# because same-origin is stricter than same-site.
#
# The Docker/nginx build is unaffected: it passes VITE_API_BASE_URL as a build
# arg, and Vite gives a real environment variable precedence over .env files.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
# Sentry DSN. Committed on purpose: a DSN is not a credential — it is compiled
# into the client bundle and visible to every visitor by design. It only allows
# *sending* events to this project, never reading them. The secret that does not
# belong here is the auth token used to upload source maps.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://c3065e2f0f8ccf0c18c9d070e13ad0ce@o325983.ingest.us.sentry.io/4511938153611264
